{
  "about": [
    "Journal events, and the OTLP bodies Observe's web, Apple and Linux services must send for them.",
    "wire.test.mjs runs the web and Apple services, host/linux/tests/observe the Linux one.",
    "Walls are in seconds. The web journal uses milliseconds, so its runner multiplies them by 1000.",
    "Bodies are compared as parsed JSON: object key order is ignored, expo.custom_params is parsed, and metrics are sorted by name, then time.",
    "Only these resource attributes are compared: the ones below and platforms.<name>.resource. The rest (os.version, device.*, browser.language) describe the machine.",
    "platforms.<name>.startupParams join every expo.app_startup.* metric's params, and launchNavigationParams the launch route's. They are each host's own launch phases and anchor.",
    "Crash records and update downloads are not here: each platform records different ones.",
    "Truncation lengths are counted per platform: graphemes on Apple, as Observe does, UTF-16 units on the web and chars on Linux. The strings here are ASCII, so the counts agree.",
    "Pinned rules: the launch route gets a navigation tti exactly when the startup event has a timeToInteractive metric and nothing navigated first; navigation params copy every exact.* field of the event; a missing url is omitted; app.error uses the event's source (default reportedByUser); exact.boot.path appears only when the startup event has a bootPath."
  ],
